# Test requests. In Visual Studio, click "Send request" above each request.
@HostAddress = http://localhost:5080

### Health check
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/health
Accept: application/json

### Database check
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/health/db
Accept: application/json

### Register — should succeed (200)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test1@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "firstName": "Ayesha",
  "profileFor": "Daughter",
  "gender": "Female",
  "dateOfBirth": "1999-03-15"
}

### Register same email again — should fail (400, email already taken)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test1@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "firstName": "Ayesha",
  "profileFor": "Daughter",
  "gender": "Female",
  "dateOfBirth": "1999-03-15"
}

### Register under 18 — should fail (400)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "young@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "firstName": "Bilal",
  "profileFor": "Self",
  "gender": "Male",
  "dateOfBirth": "2012-01-01"
}

### Register with weak password — should fail (400, needs a digit)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "weak@example.com",
  "password": "password",
  "firstName": "Omar",
  "profileFor": "Self",
  "gender": "Male",
  "dateOfBirth": "1995-07-01"
}

###

### ---------- LOGIN (Phase 2, Step 2) ----------

### Login with correct password — should return 200 with a token
# @name login
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test1@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Who am I? Uses the token from the login request above — should return 200
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Who am I WITHOUT a token — should return 401
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/auth/me

### Login with wrong password — should return 401
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test1@example.com",
  "password": "wrongpass1"
}

###
